# Client Clean Architecture Rules

## 1. Layer Dependency Direction

```
apps/LearningHub   apps/AdminPage
        ↓                ↓
@learning-hub/domain  ←──  @learning-hub/data
              ↓
      @learning-hub/core
```

- `@learning-hub/core` has zero internal dependencies — it owns `Either`, `Failure`, `Usecase`, `NoParams`.
- `@learning-hub/domain` may only import from `@learning-hub/core`.
- `@learning-hub/data` may import from `@learning-hub/core` and `@learning-hub/domain`.
- Next.js apps may import from all three packages.
- Never import upward (e.g. `@learning-hub/domain` must never import from `@learning-hub/data`).

## 2. Feature Folder Layout

Every feature (`course`, `user`, `lesson`, …) must follow the same folder structure in both `domain` and `data`.

### `packages/domain/src/lib/<feature>/`

```
<feature>/
├── entities/
│   ├── <Entity>.ts            # one interface per file
│   └── entities.ts            # barrel: export * from "./<Entity>"
├── repositories/
│   ├── I<Feature>Repository.ts  # interface only, no implementation
│   └── repositories.ts          # barrel
├── usecases/
│   ├── <action><Feature>Usecase.ts  # one UseCase class + its Params class
│   └── usecases.ts                  # barrel
└── <feature>.ts               # feature barrel: re-exports all three subdirs
```

### `packages/data/src/lib/<feature>/`

```
<feature>/
├── datasources/
│   ├── I<Feature>RemoteDataSource.ts     # interface
│   ├── <Feature>RemoteDataSourceImpl.ts  # implementation class
│   └── datasources.ts                    # barrel
├── model/
│   ├── <Feature>Model.ts  # class with static fromJson()
│   └── model.ts           # barrel
└── repositories/
    ├── <Feature>RepositoryImpl.ts  # implements domain interface
    └── repositories.ts             # barrel
```

## 3. Naming Conventions

| Artifact | Pattern | Example |
|----------|---------|---------|
| Domain entity | `interface <Entity>` | `CourseDisplay` |
| Domain repository interface | `interface I<Feature>Repository` | `ICourseRepository` |
| UseCase class | `class <Action><Feature>Usecase` | `GetCoursesUsecase` |
| UseCase params class | `class <Action><Feature>Params` | `GetCoursesParams` |
| Data model | `class <Entity>Model` | `CourseDisplayModel` |
| DataSource interface | `interface I<Feature>RemoteDataSource` | `ICourseRemoteDataSource` |
| DataSource implementation | `class <Feature>RemoteDataSourceImpl` | `CourseRemoteDataSourceImpl` |
| Repository implementation | `class <Feature>RepositoryImpl` | `CourseRepositoryImpl` |
| Subfolder barrel | `<subfolder>.ts` | `entities.ts`, `usecases.ts` |
| Feature barrel | `<feature>.ts` | `course.ts` |

## 4. Error Handling Contract

Each layer has a fixed role — never mix them.

| Layer | Contract |
|-------|----------|
| **DataSource** | Throws `AppException` subclasses only. Never returns `Either`. Throw `NetworkException` on `TypeError`, throw on bad API response. |
| **Repository** | Returns `Either<Failure, T>`. Wraps DataSource in try/catch: success → `right(data)`, catch → `left(mapExceptionToFailure(e))`. |
| **UseCase** | Returns `Either<Failure, T>`. Delegates directly to repository. No try/catch needed. |
| **Next.js API Route** | Composition root. Instantiates DataSource → Repository → UseCase. Unwraps Either: `result.type === 'right'` → `{ status: 200, data }`, else `{ error: result.value.message }`. |
| **React Hook** | Calls the internal API route (`/api/<feature>`). Reads `data.status === 200` for success, sets `error` string on failure. Never instantiates use-cases directly. |

## 5. Data Model Rules

`<Feature>Model` classes in `@learning-hub/data` must:

- Declare all properties as `readonly`.
- Provide a `static fromJson(json: Record<string, unknown>): <Entity>` factory that casts each field explicitly (`Number(...)`, `String(...)`).
- Structurally satisfy the corresponding domain entity interface (no `implements` keyword required).

```ts
// correct
class CourseDisplayModel {
  readonly id: number;
  readonly title: string;
  readonly description: string;

  constructor(id: number, title: string, description: string) {
    this.id = id;
    this.title = title;
    this.description = description;
  }

  static fromJson(json: Record<string, unknown>): CourseDisplay {
    return new CourseDisplayModel(
      Number(json.id),
      String(json.title),
      String(json.description),
    );
  }
}
```

## 6. UseCase Rules

- One class per file, paired with its `Params` class in the same file.
- For parameter-less use cases, use `NoParams` from `@learning-hub/core` (`type NoParams = Record<string, never>`).
- All use cases are `async` and return `Promise<Either<Failure, T>>`.
- Constructor takes a repository **interface**, never a concrete implementation.

```ts
// correct
class GetCoursesUsecase implements Usecase<CourseDisplay[], GetCoursesParams> {
  constructor(private courseRepository: ICourseRepository) {}

  async execute(params: GetCoursesParams): Promise<Either<Failure, CourseDisplay[]>> {
    return await this.courseRepository.getCourses({ offset: params.offset, limit: params.limit });
  }
}
```

## 7. Barrel Export Rules

Barrels cascade upward — every level re-exports the level below:

```
<Entity>.ts  →  entities.ts  →  <feature>.ts  →  src/index.ts
```

`src/index.ts` at the package root is the **only** public surface. Always import from the package alias, never from a deep path:

```ts
// correct
import { CourseDisplay } from '@learning-hub/domain';
import { Either, Failure, left, right } from '@learning-hub/core';

// wrong
import { CourseDisplay } from '@learning-hub/domain/src/lib/course/entities/courseDisplay';
```

## 8. Composition Root

`apps/<App>/src/app/api/<feature>/route.ts` is the only place where concrete classes are instantiated and wired together. No IoC container — wire dependencies inline:

```ts
// correct
export async function GET(request: Request) {
  const dataSource = new CourseRemoteDataSourceImpl();
  const repository = new CourseRepositoryImpl(dataSource);
  const usecase = new GetCoursesUsecase(repository);

  const result = await usecase.execute({ offset, limit });

  if (result.type === 'right') {
    return Response.json({ status: 200, data: result.value });
  } else {
    return Response.json({ error: result.value.message });
  }
}
```
